\pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  1\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  -2\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24   {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://bezper[0].4100/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\b\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat17 Ps.-Beda}}\plain \f1\b\lang1033\fs24 : {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://bezwrk[0].6930/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\b\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat17 Sermo in festivitate omnium sanctorum}}
\par \pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  
\par \pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 >\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24  De omnibus sanctis\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  < \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24  Legimus\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24   \plain \f2\i\lang1024\fs24 in \u281 \'eacclesiast\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  [ic]\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24  is hystoriis quod sanctus Bonifacius\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 , \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24  qui\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24   \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24  quartus a beato Gregorio Roman\plain \f2\i\lang1024\fs24 \u281 \'ea\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24   \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24  urbis episcopatum tenebat\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \u8230 \'85 \endash  \u8230 \'85 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24  si deesse contingit festis angelorum\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  ? \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24  Imitemur ergo\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24   \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24  aliquatenus sanctos\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 , \plain \f2\i\lang1024\fs24 quorum hodie festa c\u281 \'ealebramus\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24   \u8230 \'85 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24  ut quanta sit presentis diei festiuitas facilius intelligatur\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 : \plain \f2\i\lang1024\fs24 Qu\u281 \'ea tot patrociniis constat cumulata\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 , \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24  tot triumphus \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  (!) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24  coronata\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 .   
\par \pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs20   
\par \pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 Edition: J. E. \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20 Cross\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 , \lquote Legimus in ecclesiasticis historiis\rquote : A sermon for All Saints and its use in old English prose, in: Traditio 33 (1977), S. 105-120 Z. 196 (ohne diese Handschrift); Text der Handschrift stark gek\u252 \'fcrzt und teilweise abweichend (anderer Schlu\u223 \'df). \endash  BHL Novum suppl. 6332d; CPL 1368 (sermo 71); CPPM IB, 4046 (mit weiteren Autor-Zuweisungen)}

